---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { CAC_NUMBER, CONTACT_EMAIL, CONTACT_HREF, ORG_NAME } from '../lib/site';

export const prerender = true;
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How YEA collects, uses and protects your personal information." updated="25 October 2026">
  <p>
    This policy explains how the {ORG_NAME} (“YEA”, “we”, “us”), registered with the Corporate Affairs Commission of Nigeria
    ({CAC_NUMBER}), collects, uses and protects your personal information when you use
    <a href="https://www.yeaimpactfoundation.top">yeaimpactfoundation.top</a> (the “website”). We process personal data in line
    with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your email address and password when you create an account. Passwords are stored in encrypted (hashed) form, and we can never see them.</li>
    <li><strong>Google sign-in:</strong> if you choose “Continue with Google”, Google shares your name, email address and profile picture with us. We do not receive your Google password or access to your Google account.</li>
    <li><strong>Programme activity:</strong> the courses you enrol in, the events you register for, mentorship requests and messages you send, and job applications, including the CV link and notes you provide.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages:</strong> anything you send us by email.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sign-in cookies:</strong> small cookies that keep you signed in. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies, and we do not run analytics on this website.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical logs:</strong> our hosting providers record basic request information, such as your IP address and browser type, to keep the service secure and working.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To create and manage your account, and to sign you in.</li>
    <li>To send you service emails, such as account confirmation and password reset emails.</li>
    <li>To run our programmes: enrolling you in courses, registering and checking you in at events, connecting you with mentors and sharing your job applications with the relevant employers.</li>
    <li>To keep the website secure and prevent misuse.</li>
    <li>To respond when you contact us.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We rely on your consent and on the need to provide the service you asked for. We do not sell your personal information, and
    we do not use it for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share only what is needed, with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mentors and employers:</strong> when you request a mentor or apply for a job, that mentor or employer sees your name, your message or application and your CV link.</li>
    <li><strong>Service providers</strong> that run the website for us under data processing terms:
      <ul>
        <li>Supabase: account and database hosting.</li>
        <li>Vercel: website hosting.</li>
        <li>Brevo: sending our emails.</li>
        <li>Google: “Continue with Google” sign-in, and the fonts used on the website.</li>
        <li>YouTube: videos, which only load when you press play.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Authorities:</strong> where the law requires it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these providers store data outside Nigeria. When that happens, we rely on the safeguards the Nigeria Data Protection
    Act allows, such as the provider’s contractual data protection commitments.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Information we receive from Google</h2>
  <p>If you choose “Continue with Google”, we ask Google for three things only, using the <strong>openid</strong>, <strong>email</strong> and <strong>profile</strong> permissions:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name;</li>
    <li>your email address;</li>
    <li>your profile picture.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use this information only to create your YEA account, sign you in and show your name on your profile. We do not ask for,
    and cannot access, your Gmail, Google Drive, contacts, calendar or any other Google data. We do not sell Google user data, do
    not use it for advertising, and do not share it with anyone except the service providers listed above that run the website for
    us. Humans at YEA do not read it, except to give you support you ask for, for security, or where the law requires it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our use of information received from Google APIs follows the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements. You can remove YEA’s access to your Google account at any time from
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" rel="noopener">your Google account settings</a>. To delete the information
    we already hold, email us as described in section 6.
  </p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your account information for as long as your account is open. If you ask us to delete your account, we delete your
    personal information within 30 days, except where we must keep a record by law.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
    <li>ask us to correct anything that is wrong;</li>
    <li>ask us to delete your account and personal information;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent, or object to how we use your information;</li>
    <li>complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use any of these rights, email <a href={CONTACT_HREF}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> from the address linked to your account. We reply
    within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Young people</h2>
  <p>
    Our programmes serve young people aged 12 to 40. If you are under 18, you need permission from a parent or guardian to create
    an account. A parent or guardian can contact us at any time to review or delete their child’s information.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We protect your information with encrypted connections (HTTPS), hashed passwords and database access rules that let each user
    see only their own records. No system is completely secure, so please use a strong password that you do not use anywhere else.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. We will change the date at the top of this page, and tell account holders by
    email about any significant change.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    {ORG_NAME}<br />
    Email: <a href={CONTACT_HREF}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
